<div class="lens-concrete-example authority-example" role="group" aria-labelledby="{{EXAMPLE_PREFIX}}-title">
<p class="lens-overline">{{AUTHORITY_ICON}}<span>Authority in the incident</span></p><h3 id="{{EXAMPLE_PREFIX}}-title">What the agent checks before comparing the data</h3>
<p class="incident-flow-intro">For ticket {{CASE_TICKET_ID}}, the agent checks the governing meaning, its assigned job and its permission, then applies the rule within that scope.</p>
<ol class="incident-flow" role="list" aria-label="Authority checks before the incident comparison">
<li><span class="incident-flow-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span><div class="incident-flow-content"><h4>Find the accepted meaning of “complete”</h4><span class="incident-flow-record">Definition {{CASE_DEFINITION_VERSION}} · accepted (admitted)</span><p>The service owner has accepted this version for customer-data export assessments. Every required identifier selected by the account, filters and fixed snapshot must appear in the output.</p></div></li>
<li><span class="incident-flow-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span><div class="incident-flow-content"><h4>Identify the investigation job</h4><span class="incident-flow-record">Agent Assignment · Work item</span><p>The owner assigns the incident-investigation Work item to session {{CASE_SESSION}}. This records the agent’s expected participation; permission comes from the next record.</p></div></li>
<li><span class="incident-flow-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span><div class="incident-flow-content"><h4>Check permission for the next action</h4><span class="incident-flow-record">Delegation · 30-minute window</span><p>The authorized owner permits inspection of saved input, output and run logs, identifier comparison, saving candidate assessment material and preparing a change proposal. The delegation must still be current and the task view usable.</p></div></li>
<li><span class="incident-flow-number" aria-hidden="true">04</span><div class="incident-flow-content"><h4>Apply the criterion to this exact export</h4><span class="incident-flow-record">Output {{CASE_OUTPUT}} · snapshot {{CASE_SNAPSHOT}}</span><p>Compare output {{CASE_OUTPUT}} with the identifiers required for <strong>{{CASE_ACCOUNT}}</strong> and <code>{{CASE_FILTERS}}</code> in snapshot {{CASE_SNAPSHOT}}. Account membership and filter values are taken from that snapshot.</p></div></li>
</ol>
<div class="incident-flow-boundary"><strong>Keep the next action within its permission.</strong><p>The agent pauses when permission expires or is revoked, the task view becomes unusable, or an action exceeds scope. Changing source data, activating code and closing the incident each require authority for that effect.</p></div>
<details class="incident-flow-details"><summary>Inspect the exact assessment expression</summary><div class="example-formal-result"><code>Complete({{CASE_OUTPUT}}, {{CASE_SNAPSHOT}}, {{CASE_ACCOUNT}}, { {{CASE_FILTERS}} })</code></div><p>This names the assessment to perform. The accepted definition supplies its criterion; the separate delegation permits the specified investigation actions.</p></details>
</div>
